  "body": "## What changed\n\nAn empty local model field selects an installed Ollama model that can call tools.\nThe transport reads `/api/tags` and checks each candidate with `/api/show`.\nAll three local presets use this selection rule and keep their fallback modes.\nAn explicit model name remains the user's choice.\nMalformed model lists stop with a named diagnostic.\nIf no model qualifies, the message gives `ollama pull ornith-1.5:35b` and the model library URL.\nFor a local provider, the panel shows an automatic-selection hint and a clickable library link.\nAn empty cloud Model field displays and uses the shared provider default.\nCloud requests do not select an installed local model.\n\nThe automatic selection has a time limit: 5 s for each request and 20 s for the whole selection.\nThe model list request and each model probe use the remaining total time as an additional limit.\nA failed probe of one model does not stop the selection. The next model is checked.\nEach cause has its own message:\n\n- The server did not answer its model list. The message gives `ollama serve`.\n- No installed model can call tools. The message gives the install command.\n- The probe failed for a named model, and no other model can call tools.\n- The time limit ended. The message gives the count of checked models.\n\nA chat failure after an automatic selection names the selected model.\n\nOne shared table holds the cloud defaults:\n\n- Anthropic: `claude-sonnet-5-5`.\n- OpenAI Chat and Responses: `gpt-6.2-sol`.\n- Gemini: `gemini-4-hydrogen`.\n\nThe catalog test rejects a default when its table row marks it retired.\nThe table needs maintenance when providers change model availability.\n\n<details>\n<summary>UI before and after</summary>\n\nBefore:\n\n![Before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/b00d2ce26fb791475d28089e4cae74cb9fe13451/issue-3782-model-defaults/before.png)\n\nAfter:\n\n![After](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/b00d2ce26fb791475d28089e4cae74cb9fe13451/issue-3782-model-defaults/after.png)\n\n</details>\n\n## Cause\n\nThe presets used fixed model IDs.\nThe local transport did not list installed models.\nNative mode probed the fixed name and could fail before the first chat request.\n\nReadings: [Ollama model list](https://docs.ollama.com/api/tags), [Anthropic models](https://platform.claude.com/docs/en/models/overview), [OpenAI model](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/models/gpt-6.2-sol), [Gemini model](https://aistudio.google.com/docs/models/gemini-4-hydrogen).\n\n## Tests\n\nFinal head: `94478ac2b6c353808d8a277120713265dfb52367`.\nTested upstream main: `fd7ad703d5233938d1892313c1e69fa4710c99e6`.\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: RED. 14 steps: 13 passed, 1 failed, 0 stalled. 1,900 tests passed; 7 failed; 8 ignored. The UI library step failed because wgpu found no graphics adapter on this host. The timeout pins passed in this run..\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed on the final head..\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog`: passed on the final head: 39 passed; 4 ignored..\n\nPin proof for this round (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/ai_chat/transport_discovery_tests.rs`):\n\n- `ollama_discovery_caps_the_model_list_by_the_total_time`\n- `ollama_discovery_caps_a_probe_by_the_remaining_total_time`\n\nBoth slow-response pins failed with the source fix reverted. Both passed after the fix was restored.\nThe probe pin also failed with a static total timeout instead of the remaining total time.\nThat mutation took 1.5168 s and exceeded the test's 1.3 s bound.\nAfter restoration, all six discovery tests passed.\n\nEarlier fix rounds recorded red/green mutation proof for failed-probe continuation, separate failure diagnostics, the selection time limit, and the selected model name.\nThey also recorded red/green proof for the empty cloud Model default and the install guidance.\nThe latest review confirmed that those focused tests passed on `4fbbf7bde`.\nThose earlier results are not final-head gate results.\n\nHeavy lanes: not applicable.\nThe PR changes AI transport and panel code. This round changes the discovery timeout and its tests.\nThe diff changes no app operation, motion, simulation, post, or geometry code.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The example catalog suite ran on the final head. No recorded NC, CL, or catalog file differs in `git diff upstream/main...HEAD -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\" \"examples/catalog/**\"`. The worktree is clean..\nExample catalog on the final head: passed on the final head: 39 passed; 4 ignored..\n\n## Review fix images\n\nBefore: the cloud Model field shows the local automatic hint.\n\n![Cloud Model before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/f8c2b8201ee795fffa0b7f4ae1b1f5fa1657d605/pr-3799/review-fix-2026-11-24/cloud-before.png)\n\nAfter: the empty cloud Model field shows `claude-sonnet-5-5`.\n\n![Cloud Model after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/f8c2b8201ee795fffa0b7f4ae1b1f5fa1657d605/pr-3799/review-fix-2026-11-24/cloud-after.png)\n\nThe headless harness rendered these images in an earlier round.\nThis round changes no UI code. The earlier images remain above.\nNo desktop hand-test result is claimed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nLive cloud calls, a real Ollama runtime, the reporter desktop checklist, and release-only snapshot tests were not exercised in this round.\nThe transport tests use recorded loopback responses and no API key.\n\n## Reporter hand-test\n\nThe reporter tested a combined build of #3798 and #3799 on 2026-11-23 and reported NOT OK.\n\n- Cloud provider with an empty Model: fixed in `f172590ec`.\n- Ollama with an empty Model: the status showed \"Ollama not running\" while the server answered. This status text is in `settings_native.rs` of #3798. It probes the Model field text, and an empty text fails. This branch does not contain that file.\n- The automatic selection in this PR had no time limit and stopped at the first failed probe. `4fbbf7bde` fixes these two defects and gives each cause its own message.\n- This round caps the model list request and every probe by the remaining total discovery time.\n\nNot done in this PR, because the code is in #3798:\n\n- The status line with an empty local Model, and its refresh after the server starts.\n- A visible Test result and a \"Testing...\" state for Ollama.\n- The progress text during a slow first reply.\n- The panel text that says who starts the Ollama server.\n- A display of the selected model after a successful Send.\n\nKeep this PR a draft until the reporter confirms the new result on this PR.\nThe reporter must record the tested build and local preset checklist results.\nNo desktop confirmation is claimed here.\n\nUse a macOS build of this PR with Ollama running and a model that can call tools already installed.\n\n1. Open AI Chat and select Offline local (Ollama).\n2. Leave Model empty. Send \"Say ready.\" Confirm that a reply arrives without a model-not-found error.\n3. Select Local Prompt-JSON. Leave Model empty and send \"Say ready.\" Confirm that a reply arrives.\n4. Select Local Q&A (Read-Only). Send \"Say ready.\" Confirm that a reply arrives without a tool action.\n5. Select Offline local again. Enter an installed model name and send a prompt. Confirm that the name remains in Model.\n6. Select each cloud preset and clear Model. Confirm that Model shows the table default and the request uses that default.\n\n## Review scope\n\nThis round addresses only the latest review note about the total discovery time limit.\nThe required reporter confirmation remains absent. The PR must remain a draft until the reporter posts a passing result, tested build, and local preset checklist.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nChangelog: AI Chat selects an installed Ollama model that can call tools and uses current cloud model defaults.\n\nFixes #3782\n\n\n\n",
